IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc3-helpers`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4, ss 55A to 59 (part ssc3).
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-1992-4.txt, a plain-text rendering by a converter script; it is not the official text.
--
-- Shared additional pension (ss 55A, 55AA, 55B), its deferment (s 55C) and the child's special allowance (s 56).
-- Sections 57, 58 and 59 are blank in this text.
--
-- The credits and debits are the Welfare Reform and Pensions Act 1999's, which is not among the sources: whether a person is
-- entitled to a credit, what it is worth and the "appropriate weekly amount" that follows from its cash equivalent are
-- inputs. The percentage of section 148 of the Administration Act, likewise. A percentage is applied as the text says,
-- "multiplied by the relevant revaluation percentage": amount x percentage / 100 (fork F6, see NOTES.md).

§ `Part II: shared additional pension and the child's special allowance`

§§ `Section 55A: shared additional pension because of an old state scheme pension credit`

-- (7): "final relevant year" means the tax year immediately preceding that in which the pensioner attains pensionable age.
-- src:1711 | (7) In this section—
-- src:1712 | “final relevant year” means the tax year immediately preceding that in which the pensioner attains pensionable age;
@ref s 55A(7), the final relevant year (src:1711-1712)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
GIVETH A `Tax year`
`s 55A(7) the final relevant year` MEANS
    `Tax year` OF ((`ssc3 helper tax year of` (pensioner's `date of attaining pensionable age`)) MINUS 1)

-- (7): "old state scheme pension credit" means a credit under section 49(1)(b) of the Welfare Reform and Pensions Act 1999.
-- src:1713 | “old state scheme pension credit” means a credit under section 49(1)(b) of the Welfare Reform and Pensions Act 1999 (credit for the purposes of this Part of this Act);
@ref s 55A(7), old state scheme pension credit (src:1713)
GIVEN `the credit is a credit under section 49(1)(b) of the Welfare Reform and Pensions Act 1999` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 55A(7) the credit is an old state scheme pension credit` MEANS
    `the credit is a credit under section 49(1)(b) of the Welfare Reform and Pensions Act 1999`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"old state scheme pension credit\" means a credit under section 49(1)(b)" -- a definition that says "means"

-- (7): "valuation day" means the day on which the pensioner becomes entitled to the old state scheme pension credit.
-- src:1714 | “valuation day” means the day on which the pensioner becomes entitled to the old state scheme pension credit.
@ref s 55A(7), valuation day (src:1714)
GIVEN `the day the pensioner becomes entitled to the old state scheme pension credit` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 55A(7) the valuation day` MEANS `the day the pensioner becomes entitled to the old state scheme pension credit`

-- (1): a person is entitled to a shared additional pension under this section if (a) the person attained pensionable age
-- before 6 April 2016 and (b) the person is entitled to an old state scheme pension credit.
-- src:1700 | (1) A person is entitled to a shared additional pension under this section if—
-- src:1701 | (a) the person attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016, and
-- src:1702 | (b) the person is entitled to an old state scheme pension credit.
@ref s 55A(1) (src:1700-1702)
GIVEN person IS A Person
      `the person is entitled to an old state scheme pension credit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55A(1) the person is entitled to a shared additional pension under section 55A` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is entitled to a shared additional pension under this section if" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a))
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            JUST (person's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2016))
          , `the person is entitled to an old state scheme pension credit`)

-- (2): the entitlement continues throughout the person's life.
-- src:1703 | (2) A person’s entitlement to a shared additional pension under this section shall continue throughout his life.
@ref s 55A(2) (src:1703)
GIVEN `the first day of the entitlement` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
      `the date of the person's death` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55A(2) the entitlement to the shared additional pension under section 55A is running on the day` MEANS
    IF day LESS THAN `the first day of the entitlement`
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says when the entitlement ends, not when it begins
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `the date of the person's death`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST death THEN IF day AT MOST death THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the entitlement "shall continue throughout his life"

-- (4): the appropriate weekly amount is the weekly rate, expressed in terms of the valuation day, at which the cash
-- equivalent on that day of the entitlement is equal to the old state scheme pension credit. The actuarial method is the
-- regulations' under (6), so the rate that satisfies the equation arrives as an input.
-- src:1705 | (4) The appropriate weekly amount for the purposes of subsection (3) above is the weekly rate, expressed in terms of the valuation day, at which the cash equivalent, on that day, of the pensioner’s entitlement, or prospective entitlement, to the shared additional pension is equal to the old state scheme pension credit.
@ref s 55A(4) (src:1705)
GIVEN `the weekly rate expressed in terms of the valuation day at which the cash equivalent on that day of the entitlement or prospective entitlement to the shared additional pension is equal to the old state scheme pension credit in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 55A(4) the appropriate weekly amount in pounds` MEANS
    `the weekly rate expressed in terms of the valuation day at which the cash equivalent on that day of the entitlement or prospective entitlement to the shared additional pension is equal to the old state scheme pension credit in pounds`

-- (5): the relevant revaluation percentage is the percentage specified, in relation to earnings factors for the tax year in
-- which the entitlement to the credit arose, by the last order under section 148 of the Administration Act to come into
-- force before the end of the final relevant year. The orders are not among the sources, so the percentage is an input.
-- src:1706 | (5) The relevant revaluation percentage for the purposes of that subsection is the percentage specified, in relation to earnings factors for the tax year in which the entitlement to the old state scheme pension credit arose, by the last order under section 148 of the Administration Act to come into force before the end of the final relevant year.
@ref s 55A(5) (src:1706)
GIVEN `the percentage specified by the last order under section 148 of the Administration Act to come into force before the end of the final relevant year in relation to earnings factors for the tax year in which the entitlement to the old state scheme pension credit arose` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 55A(5) the relevant revaluation percentage` MEANS
    `the percentage specified by the last order under section 148 of the Administration Act to come into force before the end of the final relevant year in relation to earnings factors for the tax year in which the entitlement to the old state scheme pension credit arose`

-- (3): the weekly rate is the appropriate weekly amount, unless the entitlement to the credit arose before the final
-- relevant year, in which case it is that amount multiplied by the relevant revaluation percentage.
-- src:1704 | (3) The weekly rate of a shared additional pension under this section shall be the appropriate weekly amount, unless the pensioner’s entitlement to the old state scheme pension credit arose before the final relevant year, in which case it shall be that amount multiplied by the relevant revaluation percentage.
@ref s 55A(3) (src:1704)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
      `the day the pensioner's entitlement to the old state scheme pension credit arose` IS A DATE
      `the appropriate weekly amount in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the relevant revaluation percentage` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 55A(3) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension in pounds` MEANS
    IF `the day the pensioner's entitlement to the old state scheme pension credit arose` LESS THAN (`ssc3 helper first day of tax year` ((`s 55A(7) the final relevant year` pensioner)'s `calendar year in which it begins`))
    THEN
        CONSIDER `the appropriate weekly amount in pounds`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the appropriate weekly amount rests on a cash equivalent the regulations calculate
        WHEN JUST amount THEN
            CONSIDER `the relevant revaluation percentage`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the percentage is that of an order under section 148 of the Administration Act
            WHEN JUST percentage THEN JUST (amount TIMES (percentage DIVIDED BY 100))
    ELSE `the appropriate weekly amount in pounds`

§§ `Section 55AA: shared additional pension because of a new state scheme pension credit`

-- (4): "new state scheme pension credit" means a credit under section 49A(2)(b) of the Welfare Reform and Pensions Act 1999.
-- src:1721 | (4) In this section “new state scheme pension credit” means a credit under section 49A(2)(b) of the Welfare Reform and Pensions Act 1999.
@ref s 55AA(4) (src:1721)
GIVEN `the credit is a credit under section 49A(2)(b) of the Welfare Reform and Pensions Act 1999` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 55AA(4) the credit is a new state scheme pension credit` MEANS
    `the credit is a credit under section 49A(2)(b) of the Welfare Reform and Pensions Act 1999`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"new state scheme pension credit\" means a credit under section 49A(2)(b)" -- a definition that says "means"

-- (1): a person is entitled to a shared additional pension under this section if (a) the person reached pensionable age
-- before 6 April 2016 and (b) the person is entitled to a new state scheme pension credit.
-- src:1716 | (1) A person is entitled to a shared additional pension under this section if—
-- src:1717 | (a) the person reached pensionable age before 6 April 2016, and
-- src:1718 | (b) the person is entitled to a new state scheme pension credit.
@ref s 55AA(1) (src:1716-1718)
GIVEN person IS A Person
      `the person is entitled to a new state scheme pension credit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55AA(1) the person is entitled to a shared additional pension under section 55AA` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is entitled to a shared additional pension under this section if" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a))
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            JUST (person's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2016))
          , `the person is entitled to a new state scheme pension credit`)

-- (2): the entitlement continues throughout the person's life.
-- src:1719 | (2) A person's entitlement to a shared additional pension under this section continues throughout his or her life.
@ref s 55AA(2) (src:1719)
GIVEN `the first day of the entitlement` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
      `the date of the person's death` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55AA(2) the entitlement to the shared additional pension under section 55AA is running on the day` MEANS
    IF day LESS THAN `the first day of the entitlement`
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says when the entitlement ends, not when it begins
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `the date of the person's death`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST death THEN IF day AT MOST death THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the entitlement "continues throughout his or her life"

-- (3): the weekly rate is equal to the amount of the new state scheme pension credit.
-- src:1720 | (3) The weekly rate of a shared additional pension under this section is equal to the amount of the new state scheme pension credit.
@ref s 55AA(3) (src:1720)
GIVEN `the amount of the new state scheme pension credit in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 55AA(3) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension in pounds` MEANS `the amount of the new state scheme pension credit in pounds`

§§ `Section 55B: reduction of shared additional pension: pension sharing`

-- (8): "final relevant year" means the tax year immediately preceding that in which the pensioner attains pensionable age.
-- src:1737 | (8) In this section—
-- src:1738 | “final relevant year” means the tax year immediately preceding that in which the pensioner attains pensionable age;
@ref s 55B(8), the final relevant year (src:1737-1738)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
GIVETH A `Tax year`
`s 55B(8) the final relevant year` MEANS
    `Tax year` OF ((`ssc3 helper tax year of` (pensioner's `date of attaining pensionable age`)) MINUS 1)

-- (8): "old state scheme pension debit" means a debit under section 49(1)(a) of the Welfare Reform and Pensions Act 1999.
-- src:1739 | “old state scheme pension debit”, means a debit under section 49(1)(a) of the Welfare Reform and Pensions Act 1999 (debit for the purposes of this Part of this Act);
@ref s 55B(8), old state scheme pension debit (src:1739)
GIVEN `the debit is a debit under section 49(1)(a) of the Welfare Reform and Pensions Act 1999` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 55B(8) the debit is an old state scheme pension debit` MEANS
    `the debit is a debit under section 49(1)(a) of the Welfare Reform and Pensions Act 1999`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"old state scheme pension debit\", means a debit under section 49(1)(a)" -- a definition that says "means"

-- (8): "valuation day" means the day on which the pensioner became subject to the state scheme pension debit.
-- src:1740 | “valuation day” means the day on which the pensioner became subject to the state scheme pension debit.
@ref s 55B(8), valuation day (src:1740)
GIVEN `the day the pensioner became subject to the state scheme pension debit` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 55B(8) the valuation day` MEANS `the day the pensioner became subject to the state scheme pension debit`

-- (4): the appropriate weekly amount is the weekly rate, expressed in terms of the valuation day, at which the cash
-- equivalent on that day of the notional pension of subsection (5) is equal to so much of the debit as is referable to
-- the shared additional pension. The actuarial method is the regulations' under (7); the rate arrives as an input.
-- src:1728 | (4) The appropriate weekly amount for the purposes of subsections (2) and (3) above is the weekly rate, expressed in terms of the valuation day, at which the cash equivalent, on that day, of the pension mentioned in subsection (5) below is equal to so much of the debit as is referable to the shared additional pension.
@ref s 55B(4) (src:1728)
GIVEN `the weekly rate expressed in terms of the valuation day at which the cash equivalent on that day of the notional pension is equal to so much of the debit as is referable to the shared additional pension in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 55B(4) the appropriate weekly amount in pounds` MEANS
    `the weekly rate expressed in terms of the valuation day at which the cash equivalent on that day of the notional pension is equal to so much of the debit as is referable to the shared additional pension in pounds`

-- (5): the notional pension becomes payable on the later of the pensioner's attaining pensionable age and the valuation day.
-- src:1729 | (5) The pension referred to above is a notional pension for the pensioner by virtue of section 55A or 55AA (as the case may be) which becomes payable on the later of—
-- src:1730 | (a) his attaining pensionable age, and
-- src:1731 | (b) the valuation day.
@ref s 55B(5) (src:1729-1731)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
      `the valuation day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 55B(5) the day the notional pension becomes payable` MEANS
    IF pensioner's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN `the valuation day`
    THEN `the valuation day`
    ELSE pensioner's `date of attaining pensionable age`

-- (6): the relevant revaluation percentage is the percentage specified, in relation to earnings factors for the tax year in
-- which the pensioner became subject to the debit, by the last order under section 148 of the Administration Act to come
-- into force before the end of the final relevant year (an input, as for section 55A(5)).
-- src:1732 | (6) For the purposes of subsection (3) above, the relevant revaluation percentage is the percentage specified, in relation to earnings factors for the tax year in which the pensioner became subject to the debit, by the last order under section 148 of the Administration Act to come into force before the end of the final relevant year.
@ref s 55B(6) (src:1732)
GIVEN `the percentage specified by the last order under section 148 of the Administration Act to come into force before the end of the final relevant year in relation to earnings factors for the tax year in which the pensioner became subject to the debit` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 55B(6) the relevant revaluation percentage` MEANS
    `the percentage specified by the last order under section 148 of the Administration Act to come into force before the end of the final relevant year in relation to earnings factors for the tax year in which the pensioner became subject to the debit`

-- (2): if the pensioner became subject to the debit in or after the final relevant year, the weekly rate is reduced by the
-- appropriate weekly amount.
-- src:1726 | (2) If the pensioner became subject to the debit in or after the final relevant year, the weekly rate of the pension shall be reduced by the appropriate weekly amount.
@ref s 55B(2) (src:1726)
GIVEN `the appropriate weekly amount in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 55B(2) the reduction of the weekly rate in pounds` MEANS `the appropriate weekly amount in pounds`

-- (3): if the pensioner became subject to the debit before the final relevant year, the weekly rate is reduced by the
-- appropriate weekly amount multiplied by the relevant revaluation percentage.
-- src:1727 | (3) If the pensioner became subject to the debit before the final relevant year, the weekly rate of the additional pension shall be reduced by the appropriate weekly amount multiplied by the relevant revaluation percentage.
@ref s 55B(3) (src:1727)
GIVEN `the appropriate weekly amount in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the relevant revaluation percentage` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 55B(3) the reduction of the weekly rate in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the appropriate weekly amount in pounds`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the appropriate weekly amount rests on a cash equivalent the regulations calculate
    WHEN JUST amount THEN
        CONSIDER `the relevant revaluation percentage`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the percentage is that of an order under section 148 of the Administration Act
        WHEN JUST percentage THEN JUST (amount TIMES (percentage DIVIDED BY 100))

-- (1): the weekly rate of a shared additional pension is reduced in any case where (a) the pensioner has become subject
-- to an old state scheme pension debit and (b) the debit is to any extent referable to the pension: by (2) if the
-- pensioner became subject to the debit in or after the final relevant year, by (3) if before it. Outside that case the
-- rate stands (marginal reading (c) in NOTES.md). The text sets no floor, and none is invented.
-- src:1723 | (1) The weekly rate of a shared additional pension shall be reduced as follows in any case where—
-- src:1724 | (a) the pensioner has become subject to an old state scheme pension debit, and
-- src:1725 | (b) the debit is to any extent referable to the pension.
@ref s 55B(1) (src:1723-1725)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
      `the pensioner has become subject to an old state scheme pension debit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debit is to any extent referable to the shared additional pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the pensioner became subject to the debit` IS A DATE
      `the weekly rate of the shared additional pension before the reduction in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the appropriate weekly amount in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the relevant revaluation percentage` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 55B(1) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension after the reduction in pounds` MEANS
    IF `the pensioner has become subject to an old state scheme pension debit` AND `the debit is to any extent referable to the shared additional pension`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `the reduction`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the reduction rests on a cash equivalent the regulations calculate, or on an order under section 148
        WHEN JUST reduction THEN JUST (`the weekly rate of the shared additional pension before the reduction in pounds` MINUS reduction)
    ELSE JUST `the weekly rate of the shared additional pension before the reduction in pounds`  -- unmodified, not a "no": the weekly rate "shall be reduced as follows in any case where" (a) and (b) hold; outside that case the rate stands (marginal reading (c) in NOTES.md)
    WHERE
        `the reduction` MEANS
            IF `the day the pensioner became subject to the debit` AT LEAST (`ssc3 helper first day of tax year` ((`s 55B(8) the final relevant year` pensioner)'s `calendar year in which it begins`))
            THEN `s 55B(2) the reduction of the weekly rate in pounds` `the appropriate weekly amount in pounds`
            ELSE `s 55B(3) the reduction of the weekly rate in pounds` `the appropriate weekly amount in pounds` `the relevant revaluation percentage`

§§ `Section 55C: pension increase or lump sum where entitlement to shared additional pension is deferred`

-- (1): where a person's entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred, Schedule 5A has effect.
-- src:1742 | (1) Where a person’s entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred, Schedule 5A to this Act has effect.
@ref s 55C(1) (src:1742)
GIVEN `the entitlement to the shared additional pension is deferred` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55C(1) Schedule 5A has effect` MEANS
    IF `the entitlement to the shared additional pension is deferred` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Schedule 5A "has effect" where entitlement is deferred; the section does not say it has no effect otherwise

-- (3): a person's entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred (a) where the person would be entitled to a
-- Category A or Category B retirement pension but for the fact that that entitlement is deferred, if and so long as that
-- entitlement is deferred, and (b) otherwise, if and so long as the person does not become entitled to the shared
-- additional pension by reason only of not satisfying the conditions of section 1 of the Administration Act.
-- The deferment of the retirement pension is section 55(3)'s answer (ssc3-e-s51-s55.l4), an input here.
-- src:1747 | (3) For the purposes of this Act, a person’s entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred—
-- src:1748 | (a) where he would be entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension but for the fact that his entitlement is deferred, if and so long as his entitlement to such a pension is deferred, and
-- src:1749 | (b) otherwise, if and so long as he does not become entitled to the shared additional pension by reason only of not satisfying the conditions of section 1 of the Administration Act (entitlement to benefit dependent on claim),
-- src:1750 | and, in relation to a shared additional pension, “period of deferment” shall be construed accordingly.
@ref s 55C(3) (src:1747-1750)
GIVEN `he would be entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension but for the fact that his entitlement is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 55(3) the retirement pension is deferred` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `he does not become entitled to the shared additional pension by reason only of not satisfying the conditions of section 1 of the Administration Act (entitlement to benefit dependent on claim)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55C(3) the shared additional pension is deferred` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deferred -- (a) where ... if and so long as ..., and (b) otherwise, if and so long as" -- an "if and so long as" test in each limb
    IF `he would be entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension but for the fact that his entitlement is deferred`
    THEN `s 55(3) the retirement pension is deferred`
    ELSE `he does not become entitled to the shared additional pension by reason only of not satisfying the conditions of section 1 of the Administration Act (entitlement to benefit dependent on claim)`

§§ `Section 56: child's special allowance, existing beneficiaries`

-- (1), the rate: the weekly rate specified in Schedule 4, Part I, paragraph 6 (the table is omitted from this text: an input).
-- src:1753 | (1) Subject to the provisions of this Act ... , a woman whose marriage has been terminated by divorce shall be entitled to a child’s special allowance at the weekly rate specified in Schedule 4, Part I, paragraph 6, if—
@ref s 56(1), the rate (src:1753)
GIVEN `sch 4 pt I para 6 the weekly rate of a child's special allowance in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 56(1) the weekly rate of the child's special allowance in pounds` MEANS `sch 4 pt I para 6 the weekly rate of a child's special allowance in pounds`

-- (1): a woman whose marriage has been terminated by divorce shall be entitled to a child's special allowance if (a) the
-- husband of that marriage is dead and satisfied the contribution condition of Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 6, (b) she is
-- entitled to child benefit in respect of a child and either (i) she was so entitled immediately before the husband's
-- death or (ii) in prescribed circumstances he was then so entitled, and (c) either (i) the husband had before his death
-- been contributing at not less than the prescribed weekly rate to the cost of providing for that child or (ii) at the
-- date of his death she was entitled under an order of a court, trust or agreement which she has taken reasonable steps
-- to enforce to payments in respect of that child at not less than that rate provided or procured by him.
-- The prescribed circumstances and the prescribed rate are the regulations', so each arrives as the fact it decides.
-- src:1753 | (1) Subject to the provisions of this Act ... , a woman whose marriage has been terminated by divorce shall be entitled to a child’s special allowance at the weekly rate specified in Schedule 4, Part I, paragraph 6, if—
-- src:1754 | (a) the husband of that marriage is dead and satisfied the contribution condition for a child’s special allowance specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 6; and
-- src:1755 | (b) she is entitled to child benefit in respect of a child and either—
-- src:1756 | (i) she was so entitled immediately before that husband’s death; or
-- src:1757 | (ii) in such circumstances as may be prescribed, he was then so entitled; and
-- src:1758 | (c) either—
-- src:1759 | (i) that husband had before his death been contributing at not less than the prescribed weekly rate to the cost of providing for that child; or
-- src:1760 | (ii) at the date of that husband’s death she was entitled, under an order of a court, trust or agreement which she has taken reasonable steps to enforce, to receive (whether from that husband or from another person) payments in respect of that child at not less than that rate provided or procured by that husband.
@ref s 56(1) (src:1753-1760)
GIVEN woman IS A Person
      `her marriage has been terminated by divorce` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the husband of that marriage is dead` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sch 3 pt I para 6 the contribution condition for a child's special allowance is satisfied by the husband` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `she is entitled to child benefit in respect of a child` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `she was so entitled immediately before that husband's death` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `in the prescribed circumstances he was then so entitled` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `that husband had before his death been contributing at not less than the prescribed weekly rate to the cost of providing for that child` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `at the date of that husband's death she was entitled under an order of a court, trust or agreement which she has taken reasonable steps to enforce to receive payments in respect of that child at not less than that rate provided or procured by that husband` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56(1) the woman is entitled to a child's special allowance` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a woman whose marriage has been terminated by divorce shall be entitled to a child's special allowance ... if" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a))
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            JUST (woman's `sex` EQUALS Woman)
          , JUST `her marriage has been terminated by divorce`
          , JUST `the husband of that marriage is dead`
          , `sch 3 pt I para 6 the contribution condition for a child's special allowance is satisfied by the husband`
          , `she is entitled to child benefit in respect of a child`
          , `ssc3 helper any of`
                (LIST
                    `she was so entitled immediately before that husband's death`
                  , `in the prescribed circumstances he was then so entitled`)
          , `ssc3 helper any of`
                (LIST
                    `that husband had before his death been contributing at not less than the prescribed weekly rate to the cost of providing for that child`
                  , `at the date of that husband's death she was entitled under an order of a court, trust or agreement which she has taken reasonable steps to enforce to receive payments in respect of that child at not less than that rate provided or procured by that husband`))

-- (2): a child's special allowance shall not be payable to a woman (a) for any period after her remarriage or (b) for any
-- period during which she and a man to whom she is not married are living together as husband and wife.
-- src:1761 | (2) A child’s special allowance shall not be payable to a woman—
-- src:1762 | (a) for any period after her remarriage; or
-- src:1763 | (b) for any period during which she and a man to whom she is not married are living together as husband and wife.
@ref s 56(2) (src:1761-1763)
GIVEN `the period is after her remarriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `during the period she and a man to whom she is not married are living together as husband and wife` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 56(2) payment of the child's special allowance is barred for the period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the period is after her remarriage` THEN TRUE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A child's special allowance shall not be payable to a woman (a) for any period after her remarriage"
        IF `during the period she and a man to whom she is not married are living together as husband and wife` THEN TRUE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A child's special allowance shall not be payable to a woman ... (b) for any period during which she and a man to whom she is not married are living together as husband and wife"
        OTHERWISE FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar is stated for periods (a) and (b) and no others (a closed list)

-- (5): the condition in (4)(b) is to be treated as satisfied if, but only if, (a) such contributions are being made at a
-- weekly rate not less than the amount referred to in (3) (i) by the beneficiary or (ii) where the beneficiary is one of
-- two spouses residing together, by them together, and (b) except in prescribed cases, the contributions are over and above
-- those required for the purpose of satisfying section 143(1)(b). Which cases are prescribed is for the regulations.
-- src:1768 | (5) The condition specified in subsection (4)(b) above is to be treated as satisfied if, but only if—
-- src:1769 | (a) such contributions are being made at a weekly rate not less than the amount referred to in subsection (3) above—
-- src:1770 | (i) by the beneficiary; or
-- src:1771 | (ii) where the beneficiary is one of two spouses residing together, by them together; and
-- src:1772 | (b) except in prescribed cases, the contributions are over and above those required for the purpose of satisfying section 143(1)(b) below.
@ref s 56(5) (src:1768-1772)
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the contributions made by the beneficiary in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the beneficiary is one of two spouses residing together` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weekly rate of the contributions made by the two spouses together in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount referred to in subsection (3) in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `this is a prescribed case` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 143(1)(b) the contributions are over and above those required for satisfying section 143(1)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56(5) the condition in subsection (4)(b) is satisfied` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to be treated as satisfied if, but only if" (a) and (b)
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            JUST (`the weekly rate of the contributions made by the beneficiary in pounds` AT LEAST `the amount referred to in subsection (3) in pounds`
                  OR (`the beneficiary is one of two spouses residing together` AND `the weekly rate of the contributions made by the two spouses together in pounds` AT LEAST `the amount referred to in subsection (3) in pounds`))
          , `ssc3 helper any of`
                (LIST
                    `this is a prescribed case`
                  , `s 143(1)(b) the contributions are over and above those required for satisfying section 143(1)(b)`))

-- (4): the conditions are (a) that the beneficiary would be treated for the purposes of Part IX as having the child living
-- with them, or (b) that the requisite contributions are being made to the cost of providing for the child.
-- src:1765 | (4) Those conditions are—
-- src:1766 | (a) that the beneficiary would be treated for the purposes of Part IX of this Act as having the child living with him; or
-- src:1767 | (b) that the requisite contributions are being made to the cost of providing for the child.
@ref s 56(4) (src:1765-1767)
GIVEN `Part IX the beneficiary would be treated as having the child living with them` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 56(5) the condition in subsection (4)(b) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56(4) one of the conditions specified in subsection (4) is satisfied` MEANS
    `ssc3 helper any of`
        (LIST
            `Part IX the beneficiary would be treated as having the child living with them`
          , `s 56(5) the condition in subsection (4)(b) is satisfied`)

-- (3): where, apart from this subsection, a person is entitled to receive payment of an amount by way of a child's
-- special allowance in respect of a particular child, that amount shall not be payable unless one of the conditions
-- specified in subsection (4) is satisfied.
-- src:1764 | (3) Where, apart from this subsection, a person is entitled to receive, in respect of a particular child, payment of an amount by way of a child’s special allowance, that amount shall not be payable unless one of the conditions specified in subsection (4) below is satisfied.
@ref s 56(3) (src:1764)
GIVEN `apart from this subsection the person is entitled to receive payment of an amount by way of a child's special allowance in respect of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 56(4) one of the conditions specified in subsection (4) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56(3) payment of the amount is barred by subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF `apart from this subsection the person is entitled to receive payment of an amount by way of a child's special allowance in respect of the child`
    THEN `ssc3 helper not` `s 56(4) one of the conditions specified in subsection (4) is satisfied`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that amount shall not be payable unless one of the conditions specified in subsection (4) below is satisfied" -- the bar holds when no condition is satisfied
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, read through marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md): the bar is made "Where, apart from this subsection, a person is entitled to receive" payment

-- (6): a child's special allowance shall not be payable for any period after 5 April 1987 except to a woman who
-- immediately before 6 April 1987 (a) satisfied the conditions in paragraphs (a) to (c) of subsection (1) and (b) was not
-- barred from payment for either of the reasons mentioned in subsection (2), and who has so continued since 6 April 1987.
-- src:1773 | (6) A child’s special allowance shall not be payable for any period after 5th April 1987 except to a woman who immediately before 6th April 1987—
-- src:1774 | (a) satisfied the conditions set out in paragraphs (a) to (c) of subsection (1) above; and
-- src:1775 | (b) was not barred from payment of the allowance for either of the reasons mentioned in subsection (2) above,
-- src:1776 | and who has so continued since 6th April 1987.
@ref s 56(6) (src:1773-1776)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `immediately before 6 April 1987 she satisfied the conditions set out in paragraphs (a) to (c) of subsection (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `immediately before 6 April 1987 she was not barred from payment of the allowance for either of the reasons mentioned in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she has so continued since 6 April 1987` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56(6) payment of the child's special allowance for the day is barred by subsection (6)` MEANS
    IF day AT MOST (Date 5 4 1987)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, read through marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md): the bar is made for "any period after 5th April 1987"
    ELSE
        `ssc3 helper not`
            (`ssc3 helper all of`
                (LIST
                    `immediately before 6 April 1987 she satisfied the conditions set out in paragraphs (a) to (c) of subsection (1)`
                  , JUST `immediately before 6 April 1987 she was not barred from payment of the allowance for either of the reasons mentioned in subsection (2)`
                  , JUST `she has so continued since 6 April 1987`))  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be payable for any period after 5th April 1987 except to a woman who" (a) and (b) "and who has so continued"

-- Subject to subsections (2), (3) and (6): the allowance under subsection (1) is payable to the woman for the day when
-- (1) entitles her and none of those bars holds.
-- (A reading of "Subject to the provisions of this Act ..." in (1) with the three bars; it adds no rule.)
-- src:1753 | (1) Subject to the provisions of this Act ... , a woman whose marriage has been terminated by divorce shall be entitled to a child’s special allowance at the weekly rate specified in Schedule 4, Part I, paragraph 6, if—
@ref s 56(1), subject to the provisions of this Act (src:1753)
GIVEN `s 56(1) the woman is entitled to a child's special allowance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 56(2) payment of the child's special allowance is barred for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 56(3) payment of the amount is barred by subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 56(6) payment of the child's special allowance for the day is barred by subsection (6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56(1) the child's special allowance is payable to the woman for the day, subject to subsections (2), (3) and (6)` MEANS
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            `s 56(1) the woman is entitled to a child's special allowance`
          , JUST (NOT `s 56(2) payment of the child's special allowance is barred for the period`)
          , `ssc3 helper not` `s 56(3) payment of the amount is barred by subsection (3)`
          , `ssc3 helper not` `s 56(6) payment of the child's special allowance for the day is barred by subsection (6)`)
